"Matched" means byte-identical: a function counts only when the whole binary still hashes with it compiled from source.

## Building the decompilation

Not buildable yet: the extract and build commands land here when the build reproduces its first binary. You will need
Docker, Python 3.12 or newer, and your own dump of {{GAME_TITLE}} ({{GAME_SERIAL}}), kept outside the repository.

## Repository layout

| Path | Contents |
|---|---|
| `src/` | the reconstructed C source (`src/NOTICE.md`: no license is asserted over it) |
| `config/` | the build's records: the firewall, the references, hashes and split configurations |
| `tools/` | the project's tools, including the public-clean audit |
| `docs/` | the project's documentation; `docs/ops/` holds the operational topics |
| `cookbook/` | byte-proven code idioms, one per entry |
| `rules/` | the project's rules |
| `phase-ends/` | the record of each finished phase |

